+/// <summary>Exception-preserving calls for stripped animation playable internal calls.</summary>
+/// <remarks>
+/// Low-level wrapper integration only. Address arguments must contain readable/writable Unity
+/// handles for the duration of the call. These operations do not own graphs, synchronize evaluation,
+/// or extend the lifetime of returned data. The exception factory runs while the calling thread
+/// remains attached; it must retain the supplied native exception in the returned CLR exception.
+/// Nodes created from managed animation registrations retain the runtime until native destruction.
+/// Neither the node observer nor these calls own the backing buffers of native containers.
